From c0734a0c7a989af3ecf1770e6fa3d230ba9f0354 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lars <lars.barring@smhi.se>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 07:43:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix exact/truncated flags and symbol case in labels

- utils/codata_constants.py: cross-check worksheet is_exact/is_truncated
  against nist/<year>/allascii_<year>.json; NIST wins, with a warning.
  Fixes 62 CODATA 2022 truncated values emitted as plainly exact, and 48
  values (16 per release, 1998-2006) that were exact by definition but
  emitted as isExact false.
- nist/repackage.py: write IsExact/IsTruncated columns to the repackaged
  CSV, which previously dropped NIST's '...' marker without recording it.
- utils/package.py: restore_symbol_case() keeps symbols from the NIST name
  (u, c, hc, g, HD, HT, kPa, eV s, ...) in the title-cased prefLabel@en.
- tests: isTruncated/isExact agree with NIST for every release; exact
  derived 2022 constants are exact or flagged truncated; label symbols.

Regenerate with:
  python nist/repackage.py
  python utils/codata_constants.py --norefresh
  python utils/package.py

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
